Let neon's XML layer build against an expat older than 2.9.0.

Upstream moved ne_xml.c's two line-number calls to XML_GetCurrentLineNumber64,
which expat 2.9.0 introduced (deprecating XML_GetCurrentLineNumber) and the
bundled libs/expat has. A distribution's system expat is often older, which
has only XML_GetCurrentLineNumber -- the same value in an XML_Size. Where the
expat being compiled against predates 2.9.0, the new name is defined to the
old one, beside the existing version test for BOM handling. With the bundled
2.9.0 the condition is false and nothing changes. The two blank lines around
that block make room, so line counts are unchanged.

--- a/libs/neon/src/ne_xml.c
+++ b/libs/neon/src/ne_xml.c
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@
-
 #if !defined(XML_MAJOR_VERSION)
 #define NEED_BOM_HANDLING
 #elif XML_MAJOR_VERSION < 2 && XML_MINOR_VERSION == 95 && XML_MICRO_VERSION < 2
 #define NEED_BOM_HANDLING
+#elif XML_MAJOR_VERSION == 2 && XML_MINOR_VERSION < 9 /* linscp: system expat */
+#define XML_GetCurrentLineNumber64 XML_GetCurrentLineNumber
 #endif
-
